4) WHY PREFIX + SUFFIX MATTERS
===============================================================================

This is the MOST IMPORTANT concept from write backfill.

WHY it exists:
A follower may:
- crash
- miss writes
- restart
- rejoin later
- contain stale uncommitted entries

So leader must detect:
“How much log history does follower already match?”

That common matching part = PREFIX
Missing or conflicting part = SUFFIX

Example:

Leader:
[A, B, C, D, E, F]

Follower:
[A, B, C]

Common prefix = [A, B, C]
Missing suffix = [D, E, F]

Leader backfills suffix.

Now conflict case:

Leader:
[A, B, C, X, Y]

Follower:
[A, B, C, D, E]

Prefix = [A, B, C]
Conflicting suffix = leader(X,Y), follower(D,E)

Follower deletes wrong suffix.
Then leader sends correct suffix.

THIS is log repair.

===============================================================================
5) WRITES BACKFILL / LOG HEALING
===============================================================================

WHY it exists:
Machines crash all the time.
When they come back, they must catch up.

This is called:
- log repair
- write backfill
- suffix replication
- follower catch-up

FLOW:
1. Leader sends AppendEntries(prevIndex, prevTerm)
2. Follower checks if prefix matches
3. If mismatch → reject
4. Leader moves backward
5. Retry older prefix
6. Once match found → send remaining suffix

Example:

Leader:
1:A 2:B 3:C 4:D 5:E

Follower:
1:A 2:B 3:X

Leader sends prevIndex=5 → reject
Then 4 → reject
Then 3(term=C) → match
Delete X
Append D,E

Now follower healed.

WHY this is beautiful:
No full data copy required.
Only divergent suffix repaired.

This is very bandwidth efficient.

