12) WHY RAFT DOES NOT REPLACE 2PC
===============================================================================

This is the subtle but SUPER important conclusion from the video.

Raft solves:
REPLICATED LOG CONSENSUS WITHIN A REPLICA GROUP

2PC solves:
ATOMIC COMMIT ACROSS MULTIPLE INDEPENDENT SYSTEMS

Example:
Payment service + Inventory DB + Order DB

Need:
either ALL commit or NONE

That is distributed transaction coordination.
Raft alone does not solve cross-resource atomicity.

WHY:
Raft gives consensus inside one shard/group.

2PC coordinates across:
- multiple shards
- multiple databases
- external services

INTERVIEW GOLD:
“Consensus solves replicated state agreement.
2PC solves atomic commit across multiple participants.
These are orthogonal problems.”

Many candidates confuse this.

