14) SCALING BOTTLENECKS
===============================================================================

A) LEADER HOTSPOT
-----------------------------------
All writes hit leader.

Problem:
leader CPU/network saturation.

Solution:
- shard into many raft groups
- partition by key/hash/range

B) LARGE BACKFILL
-----------------------------------
Follower offline for hours.

Problem:
massive log replay.

Solution:
- snapshots
- install snapshot RPC
- checkpoint state

C) CROSS REGION LATENCY
-----------------------------------
Use local leader per geography.
Or async geo replicas for reads.

D) SMALL WRITE AMPLIFICATION
-----------------------------------
Too many tiny writes.

Solution:
- batching
- group commit
- pipelining

===============================================================================
15) TRADEOFFS
===============================================================================

CHOICE: SYNCHRONOUS QUORUM REPLICATION
WHY:
No committed write loss.

SOLVES:
crash consistency

TRADEOFF:
higher latency

WHEN NOT:
analytics events, logs, clickstream

CHOICE: SINGLE LEADER
WHY:
simple ordering

SOLVES:
write conflicts

TRADEOFF:
leader bottleneck

WHEN NOT:
ultra high geo-distributed write workloads

